---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { designItems } from '../data/design';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Design portfolio · Vania Sandra Clarissa"
  description="Posters, flyers, merchandise promotion and science-communication graphics by Vania Sandra Clarissa, made for student organisations, campus events and professional project communication."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <h1>Design portfolio</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Posters, flyers, merchandise promotion and infographics — most of it made while studying, and
        later for project communication at work.
      </p>
      <p class="meta page-meta">{designItems.length} pieces · 2019 – 2021</p>
      <p class="work-intro">
        These are the layouts I made, not a design degree. The briefs came from student committees and
        project teams: announce an event, explain a science idea, sell a bundle of t-shirts. Reading
        order, contrast and a single clear headline were the constraints.
      </p>
      <p class="design-notice">
        Contact details, messaging handles, phone numbers and bank account numbers have been removed
        from the public images here. Where a poster contains third-party photography or illustration,
        that is noted under the piece.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section design-section" aria-labelledby="design-list-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2 id="design-list-title" class="sr-only">Design work</h2>
      <div class="design-grid">
        {designItems.map((item) => (
          <article class="design-item" data-reveal>
            <a class="design-link" href={item.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              <img
                src={item.src}
                alt={item.alt}
                width={item.width}
                height={item.height}
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
            </a>
            <div class="design-body">
              <p class="meta">{item.kind} · {item.yearLabel}</p>
              <h3 class="design-title">{item.title}</h3>
              {item.organisation && <p class="meta design-org">{item.organisation}</p>}
              <p>{item.summary}</p>
              {(item.redacted || item.credit) && (
                <ul class="design-flags">
                  {item.redacted && <li>{item.redacted}</li>}
                  {item.credit && <li>{item.credit}</li>}
                </ul>
              )}
              {item.workSlug && (
                <a class="text-action" href={`/work/${item.workSlug}/`}>
                  Read the case <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                </a>
              )}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sage" aria-labelledby="design-about-title">
    <div class="shell timeline-grid">
      <div class="timeline-rail" data-reveal>
        <h2 id="design-about-title">Where this came from</h2>
        <p class="meta">Student committees, then project communication at work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bio-body" data-reveal>
        <p>
          Most of this was made while studying physics at Universitas Indonesia, in student committee
          roles that included promotional posters and event communications — the physics department
          association, the department orientation committee and the TEDxUniversitasIndonesia team. The
          two event posters here that carry the department's own handles are the clearest record of
          that work.
        </p>
        <p>
          The webinar poster is professional work, produced during the project management internship
          on the Fisheries Cyber Center. The coffee infographic is independent science communication,
          written and laid out by me, and the THERAFÉ mark is a concept I developed on my own.
        </p>
        <a class="text-action" href="/about/">
          The organisations I worked with <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
